# Lints after work

- **After** a coherent task or meaningful source edit: run workspace diagnostics on changed paths and fix issues you introduced. For `tentura_lints` plugin rules use `./scripts/check-custom-lints.sh <package-dir>` — **never** `flutter analyze` (does not load plugins), never `dart analyze <subdir>` (drops plugin diagnostics), and never Dart MCP `analyze_files` (spawns a second language-server and can freeze the machine). Use `ReadLints` for IDE diagnostics.
- **Before** `git commit` (or staging a commit): re-check the same scope so analyzer/CI stays green.

## `tentura_lints` (`packages/tentura_lints`)

Rules live under `packages/tentura_lints/lib/src/rules/`; register in `lib/main.dart`. Enabled via a `plugins:` block in **each** package's own `analysis_options.yaml` (root, `packages/client`, `packages/server`) — the analyzer reads the nearest options file, so a root-only block does not reach package code. CI runs `scripts/check-custom-lints.sh` for both packages (see `.github/workflows/pipeline.yml`); it wraps `dart analyze` and ratchets the custom-rule count against `scripts/custom-lint-baseline.txt`. One error-severity rule is currently switched off with a TODO: `no_map_dynamic_in_use_case_api` (server). Full wording: **Static enforcement** in `architecture.mdc`.

| Rule | One line |
|------|----------|
| `no_domain_to_data_or_ui_import` | Client `lib/domain/`: no `package:tentura/.../data/` or `.../ui/` imports. |
| `no_cubit_to_data_service_import` | Client `**/ui/bloc/*_cubit.dart`: no `.../data/service/` imports. |
| `no_map_dynamic_in_use_case_api` | `**/lib/domain/use_case/**/*.dart`: public API must not return `Map<String, dynamic>` / `List<Map<…>>` / bare `dynamic`. |
| `no_raw_graphql_in_dart` | No inline GraphQL document strings or `gql('…')`; use `.graphql` + generated `*Req`. |
| `no_inline_font_size` | Client `lib/features/**` + `lib/ui/**`: no numeric literal `TextStyle(fontSize: …)` (use `TextTheme` / `TenturaText`; allow-list `design_system/`, `rating_scatter_view.dart`, `colors_drawer.dart` — the latter is a code-level allowance for a file that no longer exists). |
| `cubit_requires_use_case_for_multi_repos` | Client `packages/client/.../ui/bloc/*_cubit.dart`: ≥2 repo params ⇒ must inject a `*Case`. |
| `no_operational_raw_color` | Client `features/beacon_view/`, `features/my_work/`, `features/inbox/`: no `Colors.*` / `Color(0x…)` (use `context.tt` tokens). |
| `no_operational_raw_text_style` | Same scope: no ad-hoc `TextStyle(…)` (use `TenturaText.*`). |
| `no_raw_edge_insets` | Client feature / shared UI: no `EdgeInsets*` from raw numeric literals (use `context.tt` density tokens / `TenturaSpacing.*`; `EdgeInsets.zero` is fine). |
| `no_raw_border_radius` | Client feature / shared UI: no `BorderRadius`/`Radius` from raw numerics (use `context.tt.cardRadius` / `buttonRadius` / `TenturaRadii.*`). |
| `no_operational_pill_widgets_in_beacon_view` | `features/beacon_view`: no `Chip`/`Badge`/`SegmentedButton` family (use `TenturaStatusText`, `TenturaTypeLabel`, `TenturaUnderlineTabs`). |
| `use_tentura_top_bar` | Feature / shared UI app bars must use the design-system top bar; plain `AppBar`/`SliverAppBar` only for immersive overlays on an allow-list. |
| `no_request_domain_entity` | No parallel `Request` domain types — Beacon stays the internal entity. |

**Baselines:** existing debt uses `// TODO(contract): Phase-2 DTO migration — …` plus `// ignore: tentura_lints/<rule>` until Phase 2 DTO work removes them.
